      "claim": "An \"executive order\" in the United States is a directive that can be issued only by the President of the United States.",
      "evidence": "3 U.S.C. § 19 defines executive orders as \"orders issued by the President\"; constitutional law (Article II) vests executive power in the President; CRS reports and Supreme Court precedent (e.g., Youngstown Sheet & Tube Co. v. Sawyer, 1952) treat executive orders as uniquely presidential instruments.",
      "weight": 0.35,
