      "id": 4,
      "claim": "John Key cannot be delegated the authority to issue a U.S. executive order because he holds no U.S. office and is not a U.S. citizen.",
      "evidence": "Constitutional and statutory requirements restrict the President’s delegated authority to U.S. officers and officials; no provision permits a foreign national without U.S. office to issue an executive order.",
